## Project: ZeroDay Security — GRC Compliance Platform

### Stack
- TanStack Start v1 (React 19, SSR on Cloudflare Workers)
- Supabase (Postgres, Auth, RLS, Edge Functions)
- Tailwind CSS v4 (configured via CSS @import, NOT tailwind.config.js)
- Vite 7

### Key Conventions
- File-based routing in `src/routes/` (TanStack Router)
- Components in `src/components/`, hooks in `src/hooks/`
- Supabase client: `import { supabase } from '@/integrations/supabase/client'`
- Server admin client: `import { supabaseAdmin } from '@/integrations/supabase/client.server'`
- Auth middleware: `import { requireSupabaseAuth } from '@/integrations/supabase/auth-middleware'`
- Design tokens defined in `src/styles.css` and `index.css` — use semantic classes, never raw colors

### Do NOT Edit (Auto-Generated)
- `src/integrations/supabase/client.ts`
- `src/integrations/supabase/types.ts`
- `src/routeTree.gen.ts`
- `.env`

### Database
- All tables use Row-Level Security (RLS)
- Roles: admin, analyst, auditor, viewer (stored in `user_roles` table)
- `has_role(user_id, role)` — SECURITY DEFINER function for policy checks
- Profiles auto-created on signup via trigger

### Security Focus Areas
- See `SECURITY.md` for known findings and review checklist
- RLS policies need tightening on `vendors`, `assets`, `audit_logs` tables
- Ensure all server functions use `requireSupabaseAuth` middleware
- Never expose service role key to client code
